From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OHOS PC Developer <ohpcd@example.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Jul 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: add OHOS fallback for curses dependency discovery

OHOS CI workers ship the ncurses static library (libncursesw.a) and
headers under /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/{include,lib} but
do NOT install a curses.pc / ncurses.pc pkg-config file. As a result
meson's dependency('curses', required: true) fails at the pkg-config
stage on OHOS:

  Run-time dependency curses found: NO

Earlier attempts:
  1. dependency('curses', required: true) → fails on OHOS (no .pc)
  2. cc.find_library('ncursesw', dirs: [...]) → meson 1.11.1 probes
     by compiling+linking a test program; under Conan's isolated
     MesonToolchain the OHOS clang default search paths miss both -I
     and -L for /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local, so the probe
     fails with:
       ../meson.build:150:21: ERROR: C shared or static library
       'ncursesw' not found

Final approach (this patch):
  Keep dependency('curses', required: false) as the primary,
  portable discovery path (works on Linux/macOS via pkg-config).
  Only when pkg-config fails (i.e. on OHOS, where curses.pc is
  absent) fall back to declare_dependency() with explicit -I/-L/-l
  pointing at the OHOS system install path.

This contract-aligns with conanfile.py's validate() which permits
os in ("Linux", "OHOS"):
  - Linux: dependency('curses') succeeds via pkg-config → fallback
           not entered, original portable behaviour preserved.
  - OHOS:  dependency('curses') fails (no .pc) → fallback
          declare_dependency() injects -L/storage/.../lib
          -lncursesw and -I/storage/.../include. No probe is
          performed by meson (declare_dependency does not compile
          a test program), so the missing default search paths do
          not matter.

declare_dependency() returns found() == true, so the downstream
`if curses.found()` header-detection block continues to run on both
platforms. Source files (src/*.c, include/*.h) do not reference any
HAVE_NCURSES* / HAVE_CURSES* macros, so missed cc.has_header() probes
on OHOS only emit meson warnings, not errors. At compile time,
static_library(..., dependencies: [curses, math]) applies the
curses include_directories, so #include <curses.h> resolves.

No source code logic changes — only the dependency discovery method.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OHOS-specific path]
Signed-off-by: OHOS PC Developer <ohpcd@example.com>

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -142,7 +142,17 @@ if is_windows
         link_args: ['-L' + deps_lib_path, '-lpdcurses']
     )
 else
-    curses = dependency('curses', required : true)
+    curses = dependency('curses', required : false)
+    # OHOS fallback: system provides libncursesw.a + headers at
+    # /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/{lib,include} but no curses.pc.
+    # On Linux/macOS dependency('curses') succeeds via pkg-config and
+    # this branch is skipped, preserving portability.
+    if not curses.found()
+        curses = declare_dependency(
+            link_args: ['-L/storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/lib', '-lncursesw'],
+            include_directories: include_directories('/storage/Users/currentUser/usr/local/include')
+        )
+    endif
 endif

 # Define some curses preprocessor symbols
